---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is there a DQ Kids Meal with a Blizzard?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. The standard Kids Meal includes a Vanilla Soft Serve Cone. If you want your child to have a Blizzard, order a Mini Blizzard separately starting at $3.49. The Mini is the right size for younger guests."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What age is the DQ Kids Meal for?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "DQ Kids Meals are recommended for children approximately 12 and under. There are no age restrictions — adults can order them if they prefer a smaller meal. The Kids Meal portion sizes are appropriate for younger children."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---
<Layout title="Dairy Queen Kids Meals Menu & Prices 2026 — DQ Kids Menu..." description="Dairy Queen Kids Meals 2026 — all $4.99. Cheeseburger, 2-Pc Chicken Strips, or Hot Dog plus Fries or Applesauce, Milk or Drink, and a Vanilla Soft Serve Cone.">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />


<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="breadcrumb">
<div class="container"><ol>
<li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
<li><a href="/#full-menu">Menu</a></li>
<li aria-current="page">DQ Kids Meals Menu 2026</li>
</ol></div>
</nav>

<section class="hero">
<div class="container">
<div class="hero-content">
<span class="hero-eyebrow">Complete Kids Meals · All $4.99 · Cone Included</span>
<h1>DQ Kids Meals Menu 2026</h1>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>Dairy Queen Kids Meals — Complete 2026 Guide</h2>
    <p>Dairy Queen Kids Meals represent one of the best family dining bargains in the fast-food industry. Priced at just <strong>$4.99 across all options</strong>, every kids combo includes four distinct components: a child-friendly entrée, a choice of side (crispy fries or no-sugar-added applesauce), a beverage (calcium-rich 1% low-fat milk or a fountain soft drink), and a legendary DQ Vanilla Soft Serve Cone for dessert.</p>
    <p>Unlike many competitors where a toy replaces food value or ice cream requires an additional purchase, Dairy Queen bundles its signature soft-serve cone right into the standard price.</p>

    <h2>2026 Kids Meal Options — All $4.99</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Kids Meal</th><th>Price</th><th>Entrée</th><th>Side Options</th><th>Drink</th><th>Included Dessert</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/kids-cheeseburger-meal">Kids Cheeseburger Meal</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.99</td><td>100% beef cheeseburger with American cheese</td><td>Fries or Applesauce</td><td>Milk or Soft Drink</td><td>Vanilla Soft Serve Cone</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/kids-chicken-strips-meal">Kids 2-Piece Chicken Strips Meal</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.99</td><td>2 whole white-meat crispy chicken strips</td><td>Fries or Applesauce</td><td>Milk or Soft Drink</td><td>Vanilla Soft Serve Cone</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/kids-hot-dog-meal">Kids Hot Dog Meal</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.99</td><td>Classic all-beef hot dog on a steamed bun</td><td>Fries or Applesauce</td><td>Milk or Soft Drink</td><td>Vanilla Soft Serve Cone</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2>Kids Meal Value Analysis: Saving Over $6.00 Per Order</h2>
    <p>Ordering each of these components à la carte quickly adds up: a cheeseburger (~$5.00), <a href="/items/regular-fries">Regular Fries</a> ($2.49), carton of milk ($1.49), and a <a href="/items/vanilla-soft-serve-cone">Vanilla Soft Serve Cone</a> ($2.39) totals approximately $11.37. At $4.99, the DQ Kids Meal cuts that price by more than half, saving families over $6.30 per child.</p>

    <h2>Nutritional &amp; Dietary Guidance for Parents</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Applesauce Swap:</strong> Choosing no-sugar-added applesauce (50 cal) instead of french fries (260 cal) saves over 200 calories and eliminates dietary sodium and fat from the side.</li>
      <li><strong>1% Low-Fat Milk:</strong> Sealed 1% white milk cartons provide 8 grams of complete protein and 30% of daily recommended calcium without the high fructose corn syrup found in soda fountains.</li>
      <li><strong>Dine-In Cone Timing:</strong> When ordering dine-in, you can ask the counter crew to hold the soft-serve cone until your child finishes their meal so it doesn't melt at the table.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is there a DQ Kids Meal with a Blizzard?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">No. The standard Kids Meal comes with a Vanilla Soft Serve Cone. If you want your child to have a Blizzard, you can purchase an individual Mini Blizzard starting at $3.49, which is perfectly portioned for younger diners.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What age is the DQ Kids Meal for?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">DQ Kids Meals are intended for children 12 and under, though Dairy Queen places no age restrictions at the register—adults seeking a lighter, portion-controlled meal are welcome to order them as well.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:32px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--color-text-muted);">
      For complete adult menus, Stackburgers, and celebration cakes, visit <a href="/"><strong>The Queen Dairy Menu</strong></a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
